    <statement><p>For the curve</p>
<p><m>y = - 19 \tan(2 x - 9 )</m></p>
<p>determine each of the following:</p>
<p>Period = <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Phase shift =  <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><em>
Note:  Use a negative for a shift to the left.
</em></p>
</statement>
    <hint><p>The normal period for the tangent curve is <m>\pi</m>.  For a curve of the form <m>\tan(Bx)</m> the period is found using the formula <m>\pi/B</m>.</p>
<p>To determine the appropriate phase shift, it is often easier to determine by factoring <m>\tan(Bx+C) = \tan(B(x+\frac{C}{B})</m>.</p>
</hint>
